WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.920
This guy sued 27 women for calling him clingy and psycho on the Are We Dating the Same Guy Facebook group.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.720
Now, a judge has dismissed his case against Meta, saying his attorney used AI to file non-existent citations.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.900
In Nico D'Ambrosio's complaint against Meta, D'Ambrosio claimed Facebook profited off of disparaging posts about him

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.880
in the group that allows members to crowdsource red flags or tea about men they're dating.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:23.900
The judge wrote,

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:29.480
These mistakes and fictitious quotations bear the hallmarks of the misuse of generative artificial intelligence.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.640
In judge speak, that is, don't waste my time.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.420
D'Ambrosio's initial attempts at suing the moderators of the groups,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.040
specific women who posted in the group about allegedly being harassed by him,

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.120
and GoFundMe and Meta floundered in court.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.800
And in 2024, in the middle of those proceedings,

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.680
D'Ambrosio was sentenced to a year in prison for tax fraud.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.640
D'Ambrosio's attorney at the time basically told the jury his client

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.500
was too dumb to do his own taxes and therefore was innocent.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:05.720
In this latest case, the judge listed many reasons why D'Ambrosio doesn't have a case strong enough to maintain meta-violated any right to publicity laws or profited off of his likeness through the Facebook group.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.640
Among them, his attorney Aaron Wallner's sloppy use of AI.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:18.540
Not only did Wallner cite cases that didn't support his argument, the only places judges could find one of the citations was in a decision that supported the opposite of the point he was trying to make.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.280
Aaron Wallner is an attorney at Mark Trent's law firm.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.140
Trent brags on his website about using AI.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.980
The court demanded Wallner, Trent, and D'Ambrosio answer for their AI-generated filings or face sanctions.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:36.300
Lawyers getting caught and sanctioned for using AI and wasting the court's time and clients' resources happen so often now it barely makes the news anymore.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:37.760
Trent's site says,

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.800
We don't just use AI for the sake of it. Every tool and strategy is aimed at one thing, winning your case.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.400
In D'Ambrosio's case, it helped lose it.
